Z||000000||CanadianGT||04-18-2001||06:13 PM||||Hi, I was wondering what cars at the wreckers I should look at to get a used chevy 350 with TPI out of???  What years as well.  I would Like to get a  V8 kit this fall from Archie, and I would Like to get the engine now, so I can rebuild it.<BR>Thanks everyone<BR>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||04-18-2001||08:26 PM||||TPI 350s were installed in 85 (86?) and later Camaros and Firebirds. Vettes, too.<BR>Be careful. Most of the TPI motors were 305s.<BR>Externally, they're pretty much identical.<BR>Try to find one that had the dual-cat exhaust system. That should be the Hi-Po version. Sorry, don't have engine codes or casting numbers. Also, in about 1990, GM switched from a MAF system to a speed-density system. Less restrictive, but less forgiving of mods.<BR>This is all ancient memory to me. Maybe someone else can fill in more of the blanks for you.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000002||Dave Gunsul||04-18-2001||08:38 PM||||Some of the 87-up 305 5-speeds could be bought with the dual cats too!<BR>A hopped up 305 can move a little light<BR>Fiero better than you might think though.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||04-18-2001||08:45 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Dave Gunsul:<BR><B>Some of the 87-up 305 5-speeds could be bought with the dual cats too!<BR>A hopped up 305 can move a little light<BR>Fiero better than you might think though.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Oooops. Wondered about this. <BR>305s did have pretty good TQ numbers, though.<BR>Sure wouldn't turn one down unless I just HAD to have a 350.<BR>The 87 and later also have a one-piece crank seal, and center bolt valve covers. Supposed to be much better about keeping all their oil on the inside. The crank seal redesign also forced a flywheel redesign. Not sure about balancing. Research!<P><BR>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 04-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||CanadianGT||04-18-2001||09:08 PM||||Thanks for your responses.<BR>As you can see from another post on superchargers I recently did, I am still not sure what to do.  I recently got in a fairly bad  car accident, and got a nice insurance claim, so I am looking at adding some power to my GT.  I just got a rebuild done a couple weeks ago on my 86GT, and am now looking at either a turbo/super charged fiero or a V8 to put in a 87 GT im looking at.  A 305 is good as well huh?<BR>I guess i have to really research this before I spend!<BR>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000005||hugh||04-18-2001||09:20 PM||||If you are going to rebuild it,It doesn't cost any more to rebuild a 350 than a 305.You can have quite a few more horses for the same money.||||reg||1
